  "hints": [
    "Make each split type a function from (amount, users, data) to one share per user, or nothing if the data is invalid. Look the function up by type name instead of branching.",
    "Floor every proportional share, then give the leftover cents one each to the first users in order. Validate everything before you write anything to the ledger. When adding a debt, cancel any debt the other way.",
    "simplify works from net balances, not from pair debts: put debtors and creditors in two lists, sort each by amount (largest first) then name, pay the smaller of the two front amounts, and drop whoever reaches 0."
  ],
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n) per expense for n participants; simplify is O(n² log n) with this simple re-sorting",
    "space": "O(members²) for the pair ledger"
  }
}
